WEBVTT

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:05.860
The second match of the
Masters Tournament Semifinals.

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:11.450
A full battle between the Champion of Sinnoh, Shirona,
and the First Champion of Alola, Satoshi.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:16.580
Although Satoshi began
by sending in Kairyu,

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:21.500
Shirona’s tactic of skillfully switching Pokémon
made short work of her.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.000
He even went on to lose Gänger.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:31.390
But while his ace, Pikachu,
fought hard to bring a comeback into sight,

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:36.390
Pikachu was shockingly taken down
by Mikaruge’s Drag Along!

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:41.730
Launching a desperate counterattack
with Uonoragon and Negigaknight,

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:45.190
he managed to drive off
Roserade and Milokaross.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:50.320
Yet he ultimately found himself with
only one Pokémon left: Lucario.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:53.620
And then, Shirona...

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:58.080
Tower over all, white wings!

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:05.420
Daimax Togekiss!

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:30.740
Daimax Togekiss!

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:35.830
Its wings are spread wide,
as if to cover the entire battlefield!

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:40.910
But what a shock! Who could have guessed
Competitor Shirona would use Daimax?!

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:44.040
It’s so huge...
even that smile feels creepy...

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:47.800
Even Pikachu had trouble with it.
How’s he gonna beat it now?!

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:51.130
I don’t think the brat boy’s
winning this, meow.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:56.720
I never imagined she would pass up
Mega Evolving Gaburias...

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.890
How are you gonna
fight back, Satoshi?

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.020
Let’s go, Lucario!

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:12.150
The bond between us...

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:15.320
Mega Evolve!

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:15.900
Let’s go, Lucario!

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:22.070
The bond between us...

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:25.200
Mega Evolve!

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:51.230
Competitor Satoshi faces
Daimax Togekiss with Mega Lucario!

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:57.190
Now, let’s see how strong
Satoshi and Lucario’s bond is.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:05:02.370
Mega Evolution versus Daimax...
Now <i>this</i> is a Masters Tournament!

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:04.370
Lucario! Aura Sphere!

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:07.580
Togekiss! Dai Jet!

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:12.540
Dive in!

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:26.390
He’s running through it?!

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:28.350
Rush in, Lucario!

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:35.690
Another unbelievable tactic...

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:44.280
Lucario!

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:49.620
Swat it!

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:59.340
It swatted Mega Lucario’s Aura Sphere
like it was nothing!

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:02.010
Daimax is so strong!

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:08.260
Oh! Daimax Togekiss’s speed
has just risen from the effect of Dai Jet!

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:10.520
We’re not done yet!
Bullet Punch!

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:12.890
Dai Jet!

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:16.110
Jump, Lucario!

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:20.360
What a powerful bound!

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:25.530
It dodged the Dai Jet
and even jumped over Daimax Togekiss!

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:36.330
It’s super effective!

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:55.690
Awesome!

00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:57.480
All right! Looking good!

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:03.740
We did it!

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:06.740
Togekiss!

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:15.540
Togekiss doesn’t falter!
What incredible endurance!

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:21.000
Oh! And the repeated Dai Jet
has made its speed rise again!

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:24.380
Lucario! Charge up your Aura!

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:25.760
Dai Jet!

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:36.020
We’re not done yet!

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:41.020
What do you think
you’re doing, brat boy?!

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:42.360
You’re gonna lose!

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:44.030
You gotta get a grip!

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:48.160
Not good! Not good!
Not good!

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:49.070
Don’t worry!

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:53.080
Satoshi trusts Lucario!
This isn’t going to beat them!

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:00.000
Lucario!

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:33.160
Togekiss, swat it!

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:44.170
This attack...
has gotta... hit!

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:02.270
Kyodai Aura Sphere!

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:13.990
Aura Sphere hits its mark!

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:34.550
Both sides are still in the battle!

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:37.810
That Aura Sphere was incredible!

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:43.060
Yeah... But I can’t believe it withstood that move...
from <i>Mega Lucario,</i> at that!

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:47.940
It’s like Satoshi is evolving,
even during this very battle.

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:51.610
Yeah. He really showed off
the strength of Aura.

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:56.910
But he’s up against the Champion of Sinnoh.
Brute strength won’t be enough here.

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:01.460
Ms. Shirona...

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:03.710
I’ve decided something.

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:05.000
What is it?

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.170
Once this tournament’s over...

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:09.300
I’m retiring from battles.

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:10.420
Huh?!

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:12.800
Ms. Shirona...

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:22.940
I’m really having fun,
Satoshi, Lucario...

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:24.980
Now, Togekiss!

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:27.480
Let’s heat things up even more!

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:37.120
Look at how well Togekiss can move,
even after taking such a big attack!

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:39.290
Bullet Punch!

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:45.620
It’s so fast!

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:49.250
So all those Dai Jets
were leading up to this after all...

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:50.000
Yes.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:54.630
And the increase in speed
will let it launch moves faster, too.

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:57.340
Lucario, hang in there!

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:00.560
Now!

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:02.430
God Bird!

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:04.600
Lucario! Shadow Clones!

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:15.650
Counter it with Aura Sphere!

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:21.870
Bullet Punch!

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:45.350
Togekiss is unable to battle!

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:46.980
Return, Togekiss.

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:52.900
You truly fought well.

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:54.650
Thank you.

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:58.530
We did it!

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:05.540
Putting its all into a Bullet Punch,
Mega Lucario marvelously tucks away the win!

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:09.630
He beat Togekiss!

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:11.670
You did it, Mega Lucario!

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:13.960
No way... He really beat it...

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:16.720
Just maybe, he might actually...!

00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:20.300
Brat boy!
Show us a “might actually,” meow!

00:12:21.930 --> 00:12:25.220
Their bond is
what let them claim victory.

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:28.440
Now, let’s see if they can do it again.

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:31.440
Win or lose,
the next bout will decide it all.

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:34.440
Don’t let your guard down, Satoshi!

00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:37.490
One more...

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.240
Pikachu...

00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:44.450
One more win
and we beat Ms. Shirona!

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:49.960
I’m glad we get to
battle together once again.

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:51.830
Now...

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:54.670
Dance in the heavens, Gaburias!

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:04.050
Now, Competitor Shirona is also on her sixth Pokémon.
We’ve finally reached the climax.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:09.440
Whoever wins this showdown
will advance to the finals!

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:32.500
Gaburias sustained damage
in her battle with Negigaknight.

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:38.590
Mega Lucario’s going right into battle again, too.
They’re on equal footing.

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:42.720
Lucario!
This is our last battle!

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:45.100
Let’s give it all we’ve got,
till the very end!

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:50.890
Gaburias...

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:55.230
Looking at Satoshi...

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:58.440
...reminds me of back
when we traveled together.

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:11.210
Everything we saw
felt brand new...

00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:13.790
The breadth of the world...

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:17.250
...and the depth of its legends
awed us...

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:22.090
When we were challengers,
ever challenging ourselves.

00:14:22.930 --> 00:14:24.340
What a time it was.

00:14:27.680 --> 00:14:31.350
We’ll be the ones to face
Competitor Dande!

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:34.060
Scale Shot!

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:41.490
Lucario, jump!

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:44.990
Bullet Punch!

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:51.750
Amazing! Amazing, Mega Lucario!
It rushes straight in without even flinching!

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:56.500
This zeal... I’ve longed for
a Pokémon battle like this!

00:14:56.880 --> 00:14:59.840
Good job, Lucario!
Follow up with Aura Sphere!

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:02.670
Gaburias!

00:15:06.430 --> 00:15:11.560
Aura Sphere and Scale Shot
cancel each other out!

00:15:13.310 --> 00:15:14.850
Lucario!

00:15:18.940 --> 00:15:21.360
She doesn’t let her guard down
for a moment...

00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:25.070
She makes every move—
every movement— purposeful.

00:15:25.990 --> 00:15:31.080
But... If I can beat Ms. Shirona...
I can get stronger!

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:32.830
Dragon Claw!

00:15:33.290 --> 00:15:34.460
Bullet Punch!

00:15:52.100 --> 00:15:56.890
What an intense exchange of blows!
Neither side is budging!

00:16:00.860 --> 00:16:02.480
Charge!

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:17.500
Lucario!

00:16:17.830 --> 00:16:19.750
Gaburias, stay strong!

00:16:21.710 --> 00:16:23.880
They’re both at their limits!

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:27.510
It’s turned into
a fierce battle of attrition!

00:16:28.260 --> 00:16:30.260
Now! Dragon Claw!

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:33.260
Reversal!

00:17:27.070 --> 00:17:29.900
Gaburias is unable to battle!

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:32.570
As such, the winner is
Competitor Satoshi!

00:17:34.910 --> 00:17:38.790
The fierce fight goes to
Competitor Satoshi!

00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:44.080
We have our finalists!

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:48.130
I won...

00:17:53.720 --> 00:17:55.800
I really won...

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:57.140
Lucario!

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:04.650
We did it, Lucario!
We beat Ms. Shirona!

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:10.110
He went and did it!

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:12.450
The finals’ll be
Big Bro and Satoshi!

00:18:12.450 --> 00:18:15.570
And it’s gonna be
an incredible battle, yeah!

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:18.080
He... He...
He made it, meow!

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:21.200
Now <i>there’s</i> an
upset for the ages!

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:25.040
He beat the Champions of
Hoenn and Sinnoh! What a...

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:28.050
<i>...Champion Killer!</i>

00:18:29.130 --> 00:18:33.550
Huh? Wasn’t our goal...

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:36.970
...commentating
to make some dough and...

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:39.560
...catching strong Pokémon?!

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:47.900
Satoshi... Well done!

00:18:47.900 --> 00:18:51.820
<i>Expanding in tow
With Lucario’s Aura...
The smiles that we wear</i>

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:02.700
Your thoughts?

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:04.290
Now I’m fired up.

00:19:04.670 --> 00:19:07.880
I better make
the finals match a blazing one.

00:19:09.880 --> 00:19:11.170
Gaburias...

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:16.260
You battled marvelously.

00:19:16.260 --> 00:19:17.640
Thank you.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:33.360
Satoshi.

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:41.200
Thank you!

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:43.700
I should be the one thanking you.

00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:44.750
Huh?

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:49.330
All the aspects
you and your Pokémon showed me...

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:53.840
You’ve made me realize
that I still have much more to learn.

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:56.340
Thank you, Satoshi!

00:19:56.880 --> 00:19:59.010
Let’s battle again, sometime.

00:19:59.010 --> 00:19:59.970
Sure!

00:20:02.140 --> 00:20:09.650
The finals are now all that remains for the
Pokémon World Championships Masters Tournament.

00:20:09.650 --> 00:20:15.610
Ranked 8th in the Masters Eight;
the First Champion of Alola, Competitor Satoshi.

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:22.160
His opponent is ranked 1st in the Masters Eight;
the Champion of Galar, Competitor Dande.

00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:26.080
Now, which one of them will reign
as the top Pokémon Trainer?

00:20:26.080 --> 00:20:30.710
Competitor Satoshi? Or Competitor Dande?
Look forward to finding out!

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:38.840
Good work out there.

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:40.390
I lost...

00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:46.140
I take back what I said
about retiring from battles.

00:20:46.980 --> 00:20:48.520
I thought you’d say that.

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:53.270
I could never quit something
so passionate and so fun.

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:57.070
I have much to master
in battling and in research!

00:20:57.530 --> 00:20:59.910
Now that’s the spirit!

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:03.740
Come on out, everyone!

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:09.250
Thank you for today!

00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:11.500
You were all really cool!

00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:15.050
Next, we’re finally gonna battle
Mr. Dande!

00:21:15.050 --> 00:21:17.380
We’ll cheer you on
with all we’ve got too!

00:21:22.180 --> 00:21:24.510
We’ve made it this far
and now we’ve gotta win it!

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:26.600
Let’s win this tournament!

00:21:34.110 --> 00:21:38.360
Having taken down the formidable Shirona,
Satoshi advances to the finals.

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:43.240
His destined duel with the undefeated Champion Dande
is nearly here!

00:23:06.180 --> 00:23:08.490
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:23:08.490 --> 00:23:15.550
I’ve got my plans for when I grow up in my pocket

00:23:08.870 --> 00:23:14.000
Urgent message from Project Mew!
Urgent message from Project Mew!

00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:16.170
Reading out message!

00:23:16.710 --> 00:23:21.650
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:23:17.420 --> 00:23:20.550
“I’m sending important data
pertaining to the search for Mew!

00:23:20.550 --> 00:23:27.180
“It may be critical for our mission’s success,
so be sure to look it over, everyone!”

00:23:21.650 --> 00:23:25.930
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:23:25.930 --> 00:23:27.190
Let’s have a fight!

00:23:27.190 --> 00:23:29.820
1. Once the battle’s done

00:23:28.350 --> 00:23:30.180
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:29.820 --> 00:23:31.930
2. And we’re laughing or crying

00:23:30.180 --> 00:23:33.430
GO FOR DREAM! Go’s Road to Mew, His Dream!!

00:23:31.930 --> 00:23:35.440
On 3, let’s be...

00:23:33.430 --> 00:23:35.440
Don’t miss it!
